content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-105 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22000, filtered-water line; P-105 is within the sodium-hypochlorite-dosed P-101 to P-106 group (C01, C16).",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: on Figure 3's required basis of velocity in mm/s RMS measured on a bearing housing, the reported 3.9 mm/s is in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation'). It is above the 2.8 mm/s Zone A/B boundary and below the 4.5 mm/s Zone B/C boundary, so it is not Zone C ('Restricted - plan maintenance') or Zone D ('Damage likely - stop the pump'). The immediate-stop rule for the highest severity zone is therefore not triggered by this reading. The measurement basis and readings from both housings still require confirmation.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature: 71°C. The manual specifies housing-surface temperature measurement, but the supplied evidence contains no numeric manufacturer alarm limit or acceptable temperature range. Consequently, 71°C cannot be classified as normal or high, and the SSP-07 requirement for a priority-1 work order within the shift applies only if this reading is confirmed to be above the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal leakage: this is a documented defect requiring mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check. For this serial number, the replacement must be the bulletin-specified HF3-450B rather than the manual's HF3-450. The active leak supports planned corrective work even though the vibration reading alone does not require an immediate emergency stop.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked seal faces are the leading documented cause of shaft-seal leakage. If the removed seal is HF3-450, also investigate the service bulletin's reported early failures on this serial range associated with a revised sleeve tolerance; the bulletin establishes a fleet risk, not confirmation of this pump's failure mode.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is a possible common contributor because it is documented as a cause of seal leakage, high vibration and high bearing temperature. Check it using the specified laser-alignment method and tolerances.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal may have run dry, which is another documented cause of shaft-seal leakage; the report does not establish whether dry running occurred.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear or over-greasing could contribute to vibration and temperature symptoms. Bearing wear is also a documented vibration cause, while over-greasing, wear and misalignment are documented high-temperature causes; do not label 71°C as high until its limit is obtained.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage and cavitation remain documented possible causes of the vibration symptom. Inspect the impeller and check NPSH during the investigation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before isolation, where safe, confirm that vibration is velocity in mm/s RMS and measure both bearing housings; classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Verify the 71°C housing-surface reading against the manufacturer's alarm limit. If the highest vibration reading is classified Zone D, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart; if bearing temperature is above the manufacturer's alarm limit, raise a P1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Electrically isolate and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC. Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, then drain and vent before line break and obtain the required line-break permit. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because P-105 is on a sodium-hypochlorite-dosed line.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C14",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework. Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the existing seal and sleeve. Apply the lifting control below if any lifted component exceeds 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While dismantled, inspect the bearings and impeller, check grease quantity and NPSH, and investigate alignment. Replace both bearings as a pair if either shows wear, noise or confirmed high temperature; 71°C alone is not sufficient to establish high temperature from the supplied evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the sleeve for scoring. Do not fit HF3-450: fit one pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, for which no seal-setting sleeve measurement is needed. Continue to inspect scoring depth and replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten the seal-gland nuts for HF3-450B to 30 Nm. For the applicable Table 5 fasteners with lightly oiled threads, tighten casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm, impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm, and bearing-housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm where disturbed. The manual's 25 Nm seal-gland value does not apply to this pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool, and perform laser alignment after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Achieve the documented tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Complete reassembly and controlled return to service under the site isolation and permit controls. Check whether shaft-seal leakage has been eliminated, repeat vibration measurements on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading. Resume the documented weekly vibration-monitoring schedule and retain any unresolved temperature or bearing findings for further work.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; mandatory replacement for this serial range. Do not substitute HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit new during mechanical-seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve — conditional part: inspect the removed sleeve and replace it if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 — conditional only if bearing-pair replacement is confirmed; replace together with HF3-510.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 — conditional only if bearing-pair replacement is confirmed; replace together with HF3-512.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "SSP-07 applies to this pump. For work inside the pump or on its seal, provide electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Provide chemical goggles and nitrile gloves: P-105 is within P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, which is chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before lifting, confirm component weights. For any component heavier than 25 kg, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. No component weight is supplied, so this control is conditional rather than assumed.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If a subsequent highest-housing vibration reading is classified in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. The reported 3.9 mm/s reading is Zone B and does not itself invoke this control.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the bearing temperature is confirmed above the manufacturer's alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift. The numeric alarm limit must be obtained before applying this trigger to the 71°C reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement: standard allowance 4.0 hours with 2 technicians (8 technician-hours).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing-pair replacement, only if inspection confirms it is required: standard allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians (12 technician-hours), additional to the seal-replacement allowance.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection conflict: manual parts identification lists component seal HF3-450, while SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits HF3-450 and requires cartridge seal HF3-450B on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-105 is exactly serial HF3-22000 and is therefore expressly included; use HF3-450B. Pumps below that serial remain on HF3-450 and the manual's Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal-gland nuts, whereas the service bulletin specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B and explicitly notes that it was 25 Nm. Because this asset is at the bulletin's inclusive serial threshold, 30 Nm governs; do not use 25 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve guidance is supplementary rather than a reason to omit inspection: the manual requires inspection for scoring but gives no rejection depth, while the bulletin supplies the greater-than-0.1 mm replacement criterion. The cartridge seal's pre-set design eliminates seal-setting sleeve measurement, not the scoring inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is AquaDyne's numeric bearing-housing temperature alarm limit or allowable range for this pump? Without it, 71°C cannot be compared with a temperature limit or used to trigger the documented P1 rule (C01, C15).",
    "Was the reported 3.9 mm/s an RMS vibration-velocity reading on a bearing housing, which housing was measured, and what was the reading on the other housing? The Zone B assessment is provisional until the required measurement basis and highest-reading rule are confirmed (C06, C07).",
    "Which seal is currently installed, what is the condition of its faces and sleeve, and is there any evidence of dry running, misalignment, bearing wear, over-greasing, impeller damage or cavitation? These inspections are needed to distinguish the documented possible causes; the bulletin alone does not prove the failure mechanism (C09, C13).",
    "Do the back pull-out assembly or any other lifted components exceed 25 kg? No weights are provided, so the need for a signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment must be confirmed before lifting (C15).",
    "Are the conditional sleeve and bearing parts actually required? Sleeve replacement depends on measured scoring depth, and bearing replacement depends on inspection findings or a confirmed high-temperature condition (C10, C13).",
    "The evidence supplies a P1 escalation rule for over-temperature but no general P1/P2/P3 priority matrix for an active seal leak. Confirm the provisional P2 planning priority against site rules and escalate if the temperature alarm criterion is met (C15).",
    "No standard labour times are supplied for isolation, diagnostic inspections, grease/NPSH checks or return-to-service testing; allow for these separately from the tabulated seal, alignment and conditional-bearing tasks (C09, C12, C15)."
  ]
}
